{"version":1,"game":"linebyline","puzzles":[{"id":"line-v1-eiffel","name":"Eiffel Tower","aliases":["Tour Eiffel","La Tour Eiffel"],"category":"human-made","country":"France","continent":"Europe","level":1,"facts":["The tower was built for the 1889 Paris World’s Fair.","Its open iron framework is a defining part of its silhouette."],"sources":["https://www.toureiffel.paris/en/the-monument/history"],"landmarkId":"eiffel","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":12},{"id":"line-v1-giza","name":"Pyramids of Giza","aliases":["Giza Pyramids","Great Pyramids of Giza","The Pyramids of Giza"],"category":"human-made","country":"Egypt","continent":"Africa","level":1,"facts":["The Giza pyramids belong to the ancient funerary landscape near Memphis.","The pyramid fields extend from Giza to Dahshur."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/86/"],"landmarkId":"giza","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":10},{"id":"line-v1-fuji","name":"Mount Fuji","aliases":["Mt Fuji","Fujisan","Fuji","Fuji-san"],"category":"natural","country":"Japan","continent":"Asia","level":1,"facts":["Fujisan is a stratovolcano and a longstanding pilgrimage destination.","Its snow-capped profile has inspired generations of artists."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1418/"],"landmarkId":"fuji","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":9},{"id":"line-v1-uluru","name":"Uluru","aliases":["Ayers Rock","Uluṟu"],"category":"natural","country":"Australia","continent":"Oceania","level":1,"facts":["Uluru is sacred to the Anangu, its traditional owners.","The monolith rises above the sandy plains of central Australia."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/447/"],"landmarkId":"uluru","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":11},{"id":"line-v1-taj","name":"Taj Mahal","aliases":["The Taj Mahal"],"category":"human-made","country":"India","continent":"Asia","level":2,"facts":["Shah Jahan commissioned this marble mausoleum in memory of his wife.","The monument stands in Agra."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/252/"],"landmarkId":"taj","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":13},{"id":"line-v1-liberty","name":"Statue of Liberty","aliases":["Liberty Enlightening the World","Lady Liberty","The Statue of Liberty"],"category":"human-made","country":"United States","continent":"North America","level":2,"facts":["The statue was a gift from the people of France.","It became a symbol of welcome for immigrants arriving by sea."],"sources":["https://www.nps.gov/articles/000/statue-of-liberty-national-monument-world-heritage-site.htm"],"landmarkId":"liberty","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":12},{"id":"line-v1-delicate","name":"Delicate Arch","aliases":["The Delicate Arch"],"category":"natural","country":"United States","continent":"North America","level":2,"facts":["This freestanding arch is in Arches National Park, Utah.","Its historic nicknames include Cowboy’s Chaps."],"sources":["https://www.nps.gov/arch/planyourvisit/delicate-arch.htm"],"landmarkId":"delicate","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":11},{"id":"line-v1-table","name":"Table Mountain","aliases":["Tafelberg","Table Mountain Cape Town"],"category":"natural","country":"South Africa","continent":"Africa","level":2,"facts":["Its long, level summit overlooks Cape Town.","The summit plateau is about three kilometres long."],"sources":["https://www.capetown.travel/explore-cape-towns-iconic-table-mountain/"],"landmarkId":"table","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":11},{"id":"line-v1-sydney","name":"Sydney Opera House","aliases":["The Sydney Opera House","Opera House Sydney"],"category":"human-made","country":"Australia","continent":"Oceania","level":3,"facts":["The building opened in 1973.","Jørn Utzon designed its interlocking vaulted roof shells."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/166/"],"landmarkId":"sydney","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":11},{"id":"line-v1-redeemer","name":"Christ the Redeemer","aliases":["Cristo Redentor","Christ Redeemer","The Christ Redeemer Statue"],"category":"human-made","country":"Brazil","continent":"South America","level":3,"facts":["The statue stands atop Corcovado in Rio de Janeiro.","The Art Deco monument opened in 1931."],"sources":["https://riotur.rio/en/que_fazer/christtheredeemer/"],"landmarkId":"redeemer","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":11},{"id":"line-v1-halfdome","name":"Half Dome","aliases":["Yosemite Half Dome","Halfdome"],"category":"natural","country":"United States","continent":"North America","level":3,"facts":["This granite formation is a landmark of Yosemite National Park.","Its rounded summit contrasts with a steep, nearly vertical face."],"sources":["https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/how-did-half-dome-massive-rock-monument-yosemite-national-park-acquire-its-unique-shape?page=1"],"landmarkId":"halfdome","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":10},{"id":"line-v1-matterhorn","name":"Matterhorn","aliases":["The Matterhorn","Monte Cervino","Cervino","Mont Cervin"],"category":"natural","country":"Switzerland and Italy","continent":"Europe","level":3,"facts":["The mountain rises on the Swiss–Italian border.","Its sharply pointed profile is a symbol of the Swiss Alps."],"sources":["https://www.myswitzerland.com/en/destinations/matterhorn-symbol-for-switzerland/"],"landmarkId":"matterhorn","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":10},{"id":"line-v1-greatwall","name":"Great Wall of China","aliases":["The Great Wall","Great Wall","Changcheng","Wanli Changcheng"],"category":"human-made","country":"China","continent":"Asia","level":4,"facts":["Earlier defensive walls were joined under Qin Shi Huang.","Construction and rebuilding continued into the Ming dynasty."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/438/"],"landmarkId":"greatwall","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":12},{"id":"line-v1-pisa","name":"Leaning Tower of Pisa","aliases":["Tower of Pisa","Pisa Tower","Torre di Pisa","Torre Pendente di Pisa"],"category":"human-made","country":"Italy","continent":"Europe","level":4,"facts":["The tower is the cathedral’s campanile, or bell tower.","It is part of Pisa’s Piazza del Duomo monument group."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/395/"],"landmarkId":"pisa","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":16},{"id":"line-v1-causeway","name":"Giant’s Causeway","aliases":["Giant's Causeway","Giants Causeway","The Giants Causeway"],"category":"natural","country":"United Kingdom (Northern Ireland)","continent":"Europe","level":4,"facts":["The coast contains roughly 40,000 basalt columns.","The columns formed through ancient volcanic activity."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/369/"],"landmarkId":"causeway","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":26},{"id":"line-v1-victoria","name":"Victoria Falls","aliases":["Mosi-oa-Tunya","Mosi oa Tunya","Mosi Oa Tunya Falls"],"category":"natural","country":"Zambia and Zimbabwe","continent":"Africa","level":4,"facts":["The Zambezi River plunges into a series of basalt gorges here.","The spray can be visible from many kilometres away."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/509/"],"landmarkId":"victoria","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":15},{"id":"line-v1-burj","name":"Burj Khalifa","aliases":["The Burj Khalifa","Khalifa Tower"],"category":"human-made","country":"United Arab Emirates","continent":"Asia","level":5,"facts":["The skyscraper in Dubai opened in January 2010.","Its stepped profile narrows into a long central spire."],"sources":["https://www.emaar.com/en/other-emaar-businesses/burj-khalifa"],"landmarkId":"burj","game":"linebyline","version":1,"total":15},{"id":"line-v1-moai","name":"Moai of Rapa Nui","aliases":["Moai","Easter Island Statues","Rapa Nui Moai","Moai Statues","Easter Island Moai"],"category":"human-made","country":"Chile (Rapa Nui)","continent":"Oceania","level":5,"facts":["Rapa Nui is also known as Easter Island.","The island’s Polynesian society erected monumental stone figures called moai."],"sources":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/715/"],"landmarkId":"moai","game":"linebyline"